      "writtenOn": "2022-05-19T00:36:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems a lot of duplication for one config item (notwithstanding using a DTS include to keep the common stuff, even though it is referenced using 2 different files).\nWould it work to keep the same board name (i.e keep using it8xxx2), and use CONFIG_SOC_IT81202 for corsola and CONFIG_SOC_IT81302 for nereid?\nThen instead of using CONFIG_SOC_IT8XXX2_GPIO_GROUP_K_L_DEFAULT_PULL_DOWN, CONFIG_SOC_IT81202 could be used to disable those pins (in Zephyr itself, not in our board files).\nTo me, the CONFIG_SOC_IT8XXX2_GPIO_GROUP_K_L_DEFAULT_PULL_DOWN should really be something set via a variant name, not a config attribute (I mean, is this ever used on a IT81302, and ever _not_ used on a IT81202?).\nGiven these groups are not brought out on pins on a IT81202, should they even be in the device tree? or is it enough just to turn them off this way?",
      "parentUuid": "8e56b7c1_f96e9af6",
      "revId": "e2b55489f567e8405050d7cfa1fad1d7bee94892",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
