      "writtenOn": "2022-05-19T08:29:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can use *_defconfig to enable corresponding configurations if we explicitly define chip variant in BUILD.py (although the configurations are mostly duplicated). We won\u0027t need to enable e.g CONFIG_SOC_IT81202BX, CONFIG_SOC_IT81302BX, or CONFIG_SOC_IT81302CX... on each project. Project just need to select the correct chip variant in the BUILD.py.\n\nThe CONFIG_SOC_IT81202 can be used to disable L and K groups.\nWe can enable it in it81202bx_defconfig once upstream change ready.",
      "parentUuid": "8b567cf6_2c97823c",
      "revId": "e2b55489f567e8405050d7cfa1fad1d7bee94892",
